g":"BigInt with checked fixed-width arithmetic; usize/isize assume 64 bits","assumptions":["Rust integer arithmetic uses checked overflow behavior (debug/test profile); release wrapping arithmetic is outside this draft contract","String case conversion depends on the source and host Unicode tables","Concrete admitted constants require bounded checked evaluation with original parser source links; const fn runtime eligibility alone proves no all-input compile-time behavior","Immutable strings encode scalar values; monomorphic tagged values encode Option/Result; vectors/slices are immutable arrays"],"observation":"checked value results, local scalar mutation, immutable constructors, lazy future polling and named host effects; carried items supply no executable behavior"},"counts":{"executable":0,"executableFunctions":0,"executableConstants":0,"executableTypes":0,"executableConstructors":0,"carried":6,"preserved":7},"items":[{"term":"trivia","name":null,"span":{"start":0,"end":539,"unit":"utf16","byteStart":0,"byteEnd":541},"sha256":"a365b57c2eb6ce02adeae8d32084694d27cb9533c533fc678db4ddc5b07b97fb","source":"//! The protocol journal: what a token exchange looked like, never what it carried.\n//!\n//! These OAuth endpoints are undocumented, change without notice, and attest\n//! their clients — so a refresh that works in one particular shape and fails in\n//! another is a thing an operator must be able to see from the log alone,\n//! without a packet capture (issue #239).\n//!\n//! Everything here records *shape*: method, URL, header names with their\n//! non-secret values, and body field names. Values are the secrets and are\n//! never written.\n\n","status":"preserved","diagnostic":null,"comment":true},{"term":"use","name":"super","span":{"start":539,"end":578,"unit":"utf16","byteStart":541,"byteEnd":580},"sha256":"ec8d4f3e8a13f4e3565bdf49bb87fe16a59a4adbf3e8ea1dbd3fd888e3e7320d","source":"use super::{BodyStyle, refresh_config};","status":"carried","diagnostic":{"kind"